WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This has been
a fantastic year for you.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.736 line:92%
"Logan" was, for my money,

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the great
superhero movies of all time.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.239 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You and Hugh Jackman.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.907
And he said it was
his last time playing Wolverine,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.377
and then you announced
that it would be your last time

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.012 line:92%
playing Professor Xavier.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It was unexpected.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.482 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I did not plan that,

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we were at,
what was for me,

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
my first public screening
at the Berlin Film Festival.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.722 line:92%
I was sitting alongside Hugh,

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the last five
or six minutes of the movie

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.693 size:75% position:38% line:92%
are quite emotional.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very much so.
-And sad.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:32.966
And at one point, Hugh just
reached over and took my hand

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.167 line:92%
and squeezed it like this.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:38.872
And I thought, when the movie
ended and the credits rolled --

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had to sit and wait there
for a long time

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:42.642 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as the credits rolled.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realized there can be
no better way,

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
no more appropriate way
to say farewell

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:52.352
to the X-Men franchise
than the scenes I've just seen.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.687
And so, the next morning,
I made the announcement

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:58.358 size:84% position:42%
at the press conference
that I was done, too.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.426 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's wonderful.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is --
You are right.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is the perfect exit
for the --

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nevertheless,
the franchise will go on

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.965 line:92%
without me and Hugh Jackman.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, there's
the wonderful James McAvoy,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.003 size:84% position:42% line:92%
who plays young Xavier.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Scoffs ] Yeah.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.573 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm. Okay.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't --
You don't seem to hold him

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.278 line:92%
in the same esteem that I do.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have enormous respect
for James McAvoy.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.248 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He's a brilliant actor.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He played --
He was the young poop emoji

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.552 line:92%
in that clip, as well, right?

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's right!
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.022 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
Only, in his case,
that was perfect casting.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.995 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-When -- When he --

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.598 size:81% position:41%
When it was announced
that he was gonna play

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.901
the young Charles Xavier, he was
on a red carpet somewhere,

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he said,
"So, tell me, how does --

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does it feel
to be going into the shoes,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
albeit the younger shoes,
of Patrick Stewart?"

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:52.479 line:92%
And James said, "I'll bury him."

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good man, yes.
I'd vote for that.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.851 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's outstanding.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:58.618 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And they're already --

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:02.555
I was shooting in Montreal
the last few -- five weeks,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the next "X-Men" movie
is in the works.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:05.792 line:92%
-Yeah, it's very exciting.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I will say, one of
the things about "Logan" --

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.761 size:88% position:44% line:92%
not a film for children.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a very violent --
It was R-rated.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.065 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You got to curse a bit,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
which must have been fun
for Professor X.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:19.405
-Well, it was all a part of
the loosening of Charles' mind,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
Charles, who was
a significant intellectual

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.878 line:92%
in every aspect of his life.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
Brilliant thinker,
brilliant analyst,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:31.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
has had so much disturbance
in his life.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.520 size:78% position:39%
But one of the things
that has collapsed

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.554 line:92%
is his brilliant language.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now he uses coarse,
abusive words.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.725 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It was great to watch.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, of course,
then children can't watch.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have four grandchildren,
and --

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.696 line:92%
-Nope, they haven't seen it.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They haven't seen it.
-No.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But are they excited about
the "Emoji" film?

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They are.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
And are they excited --
Let me follow up.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Are they excited --

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:56.009
Do they know your casting,
and are they excited about that?

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.877 line:92%
-They do, because someone

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
told my grandson, Sebastian,
at school.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did you know?
Did you know?

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your granddad's
gonna be playing poop!"

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my daughter-in-law
called me and said,

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.757 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"You will never believe

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:15.528
with what excitement he came
home and gave us that news."

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said,
"Please tell me it's true..."

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.801 line:92%
"...because he is so excited."

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, they are looking forward
to this movie very much.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is entirely suitable
for them

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.675 line:92%
and, in fact, for all children.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:29.542 size:88% position:44% line:92%
'Cause it's a fun movie,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it has an underlying,
quite serious theme

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.282
about being different and how
you want to celebrate that.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:36.916 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's fantastic.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.586
And it really is always just
such a joy to have you here.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.420 line:92%
Please come back anytime.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much.
-I would love to.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.424 line:92%
-Patrick Stewart, everybody!

